es with each  new technological brain breakthrough and  Walt Disney by the way started that with  when he first started working with even  Steamboat Willie there was always  technological breakthroughs associated  the underwater sequence of Pinocchio  it's been part of it's been part of the  the game  from the beginning you want to tell  great stories but have new new  techniques right now the big  breakthrough for us was VR but VR is  really built around a game engine in the  case of doing the virtual production for  Lion King we use the Unity engine system  Magno puces a company that helped us  build a multiplayer vr filmmaking game  so that we could take our digital  environments digital animated characters  and actually go in there with the film  crew into the VR space and so the VR was  used for us to visualize and basically  create a template for the shots that  were cut together for the final film and  the mandalorian because we're doing  live-action production we're using we're  using the epic gaming game engine and  using that to do real-time in-camera  visual effects and so if you visited the  set for the mandalorian you would have  seen a completely video wall wrapped  stage and we were in there filming the  characters in the foreground and  oftentimes either blue screen or full  digital versions of set extensions in  the background with parallax because the  positional data of the camera was  informing the backgrounds and so it was  like a translate that had perspective  and so that allowed us to have  environments as long as we could build  them digitally and put enough work into  planning it we could have the game  engine be used for creating effects in a  time frame that allows us to get a TV  season done but all of that requires us  to use the same v-cam techniques in  pre-production on the mandalorian so  that we know exactly what we need to see  and so if you visited the set now as  we're starting to get into season 2 it  looks a lot like the set o